Z||000012||Raydar||09-23-2001||03:46 PM||||FWIW, the 4.10 4-speed carried the RPO code "M19", and was available in the 84 SE. The "economy" 84 did not have the 4.10.<BR>I've heard other folks say that a plain old (Non-4.10) 4 speed, behind a V-6, had better acceleration than a Getrag 5 speed. <P>If you were to go with an Isuzu 5 speed, I understand that they have perfect gear spacing for the V-6's power. <BR>Since you are on a budget, I would recommend the 4 speed. (Sounds like that's where you're going, anyway. I'll shut up now.)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
