Z||000019||c m west||09-24-2001||01:11 AM||||with 4:10 gears and just about any tire size, the engine will be screaming at 3200 - 3500 rpm at 60 mph, if you want the 4:10 gear<BR> set I have one here, if you want a stock trans ( my suggestion ) I can get my hands on one, or call George at the Fiero Shop - they have nearly 30 cars outback ready to strip||||reg||1
Z||000020||Leper||09-24-2001||01:29 AM||||Depending on what part of the case cracked, you might be able to get away with JB Welding the crack closed.<BR>Either of the 84 4 speeds would fit if you really do have a 4:10 4 speed in your car. If a 2.5 can move from a dead stop with the economy geared trans, the 3.4 shouldn't have a problem with it. You might be able to use the v6 transmission with the 4:10 cables too.(I can't remember what the 84 cables look like anymore so I won't say that it's a fact)<BR>||||reg||1
